no-debug-print: ENABLE_TPM_DEBUG_PRINT = NO

Classification: platform setting.

Simulation builds route TPM_DEBUG_PRINT strings to the platform's debug
output. The reference process must stay quiet (its stdout is redirected to
stderr to protect the harness's pipe protocol), so debug printing is
disabled.

diff --git a/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmBuildSwitches.h b/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmBuildSwitches.h
--- a/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmBuildSwitches.h
+++ b/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmBuildSwitches.h
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@
 // ENABLE_TPM_DEBUG_PRINT enables arbitrary string printing.
 // enables the TPM_DEBUG_PRINT macro to route debugging strings
 // to the _plat_debug_out function
-#define ENABLE_TPM_DEBUG_PRINT      (YES * SIMULATION)
+#define ENABLE_TPM_DEBUG_PRINT      NO
 
 //  ENABLE_TPM_DEBUG_TRACE enables code tracing macros - depends on TPM_DEBUG_PRINT
 #define ENABLE_TPM_DEBUG_TRACE      (NO  * ENABLE_TPM_DEBUG_PRINT)
